cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in authorized research, please cite it as below."
title: "Docking Suite: an umbrella platform for structure-based antiparasitic screening"
abstract: >-
  A campaign-oriented platform for protein–ligand virtual screening of antiparasitic
  targets. Each campaign declares its own targets, ligands, target–ligand pairs and
  protocols in a versioned registry, so that the peculiarities of a given system
  (oligomeric state required by the site, mandatory cofactor, macrocycle flexibility,
  reference co-crystal for redocking) are configuration rather than assumptions baked
  into scripts. It wraps AutoDock Vina, OpenMM molecular dynamics, HADDOCK3 restraint
  docking and Boltz-2 structure prediction behind one engine interface, with ADMET,
  toxicity and drug-design modules and a Flask dashboard. The repository contains code
  and declarative configuration only; no research results are distributed with it.
